# Normalize line endings for text files so Windows/macOS/Linux checkouts
# and commits can't silently disagree with each other.
* text=auto eol=lf

# backend/requirements.txt is machine-generated by `pip-compile` (see
# Makefile: `make lock`). lock-check diffs it byte-for-byte against a
# fresh scratch compile, so anything that can alter its bytes on checkout
# or commit — CRLF conversion, a missing trailing newline picked up by an
# editor/IDE save, autocrlf differences across OSes — makes CI fail on
# a file that never actually changed content. Pin it explicitly rather
# than relying on the `* text=auto` default above.
backend/requirements.txt text eol=lf
backend/requirements.in text eol=lf
backend/requirements-dev.txt text eol=lf